  "id": "COMPOUND:36014 - PROTEIN:1107",
  "verbalization": "Jasplakinolide Z1 is shown to have a direct target relationship with Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf through three distinct pathways. Each pathway involves Jasplakinolide Z1 binding to a different protein, which in turn targets B-raf. The first pathway links Jasplakinolide Z1 to Integrin alpha-4, which is targeted by a specific compound, and this compound subsequently targets B-raf. The second pathway connects Jasplakinolide Z1 to Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which is also targeted by another compound, and this compound targets B-raf. The third pathway involves Jasplakinolide Z1 directly targeting Ephrin type-B receptor 4, which is targeted by a third compound, and this compound targets B-raf. All three pathways demonstrate a consistent mechanism of action where the compound targets a protein that in turn targets B-raf. The scores across all three paths are similar, suggesting a robust and consistent relationship. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Jasplakinolide Z1 and B-raf through a series of intermediate targets, reinforcing the possibility of a biological role in disease.",
